en missing):"},"187":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-24","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#quick-start","content":"Inside `docs-site/` the same things are npm scripts: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`,\n`npm run visual`, `npm run nav:check`.  Screenshot baselines are refreshed with\n`bazelisk run //docs-site:visual-linux -- --update` (needs Docker), which renders them in the\nLinux image that matches the docs CI job — never on a laptop.  See `bazelisk run //docs:status`\nor the `--help` output for all options."},"188":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-25","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Sidebar groups live in `docs-site/lib/nav.json`, transcribed once from the former\n`mkdocs.yml` nav.  That file is gone, so `nav.json` is the source of truth: edit it by hand\nand verify with `npm run nav:check` (which fails if an entry has no page on disk).  The\ngroups are:"},"189":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-26","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Home** — path cards, default stack, safety table"},"190":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-27","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Start** — gold path, topology, profiles, learn-the-lab"},"191":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-28","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Concepts** — architecture, NCCL, Resource Guard, stacks, glossary"},"192":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-29","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Operate** — catalogs, dashboard, runbooks, troubleshooting"},"193":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-30","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Reference** — project conventions, docs contributing, generated shell + dashboard API"},"194":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-31","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Contribute** — dev environment, Bazel"},"195":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-32","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Every major section has an `index.md`. Keep existing published slugs (`getting-started`,\n`architecture`, …): the route is the file path without its extension, so renaming a file\nbreaks every bookmark and README link to it. Put **new** pages under `start/`, `learn/`,\n`concepts/`, `operate/`, `contribute/`."},"196":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-33","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"A new page needs three things or it will not appear in the sidebar and the coverage gate\nfails: the file under `docs/`, an entry in the nav (see above), and a listing in\n`_HAND_WRITTEN_MD` in `docs/BUILD.bazel` so Bazel ships it as a runfile."},"197":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-34","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Use the right-hand ToC for long pages. Keep navigation focused."},"198":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-35","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CO